# Page feature isolation

For CRUD/list pages under `client/src/pages/`, keep UI pieces in **named folders** with co-located `.tsx` + `.scss`. Do not put table, add form, and page chrome in one large `index.tsx`.

## Layout

```
pages/{Feature}/
  index.tsx                 # list / main screen only (route entry)
  {Feature}.scss            # page layout (header, search, chrome)
  Add{Entity}/
    Add{Entity}.tsx         # add/edit Modal + antd Form + mutations
    Add{Entity}.scss
  {Entity}List/
    {Entity}List.tsx        # antd Table (+ empty/actions columns)
    {Entity}List.scss
```

Examples: `AddDoctor`, `AddHospital`, `DoctorList`, `HospitalList`.

## Rules

- **Only** the page entry may be `index.tsx`. Child folders use named files (`AddDoctor.tsx`, not `index.tsx`).
- `index.tsx` owns search, query params, pagination state, delete, and open/close of the add form — keep it thin.
- Lists use **antd `Table` (desktop)** + **antd `Card` (mobile)** inside `{Entity}List`.
- Forms use **antd `Form`** inside `Add{Entity}` — no `react-hook-form`.
- Every list/form folder must include matching `.scss` next to the `.tsx`.
- Prefer plain className strings with co-located SCSS. Do not use `styles['...']` unless the file imports a CSS module.

## ❌ Bad

```tsx
// pages/Doctors/index.tsx — everything inline + custom rows
function DoctorCard() { /* ... */ }
function DoctorRow() { /* ... */ }
function DoctorsPage() {
  // form + fake table + list all here
}
```

## ✅ Good

```tsx
// pages/Doctors/index.tsx
import DoctorList from './DoctorList/DoctorList';
import AddDoctor from './AddDoctor/AddDoctor';
```
